@startuml SAYCEP_A4_Activity
' Assignment 4 Q3.2 - the demonstrated workflow, with decisions, alternative
' paths and the emerging-technology step.
title Demonstrated workflow: from skills to a saved pathway
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FEFEFE

start
:Open SAYCEP (welcome screen);
if (Have a plan code?) then (yes)
  repeat
    :Type the plan code;
  repeat while (Six characters and a match?) is (no - button disabled, or\n"No plan matches that code") not (yes)
  :Open the saved plan (dashboard);
  stop
else (no - I'm new)
endif

:Choose starting point\n(student or school-leaver);
repeat
  :Tick the skills you hold (of 35);
repeat while (At least one ticked?) is (no - Continue disabled) not (yes)
if (Create profile accepted?) then (no - validation error)
  #FBEAEA:Show error banner;
  stop
endif

#D6E8F5:Rank occupations by mean-centred cosine similarity;
note right
  Emerging-technology step.
  Input: the 35-number skill vector.
  Output: ranked jobs, each with
  the skills that lifted it.
end note
:Open a job (recommended, browse or search);
if (Aim for this job?) then (no)
  :Choose another;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

:Record the target;
if (Any must-have skill missing?) then (no)
  :Report that every must-have is held;
else (yes)
  :Classify each missing skill\nas essential (3.5 or more) or desirable;
endif
:Generate the pathway: three steps plus the target;
:Save as my plan (plan code issued);

while (Keep going?) is (yes)
  :Mark a skill "learning" or "can do it now",\nor check a CV, practise an interview,\nor read what employers ask for;
  if (Skill marked "can do it now"?) then (yes)
    :Recalculate readiness; show what it unlocked;
  else (no)
    :Nothing changes - learning does not close a gap;
  endif
endwhile (no)
stop
@enduml
